Z||000000||Zorba||10-16-2000||01:35 AM||||Will this water pump set up work? It doesn't look like the water pump bracket would fit if the pump is turned <B>upside down.</B><BR>[IMG]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/71063750.jpg<BR>[/IMG]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rprevo||10-16-2000||03:28 PM|||| I think the waterpump alt Brkt will work<BR>but the thing I wonder about is that the<BR>Little water inlet boss sitting at 12:00 when it <BR>get's turned upside down becomes 6:00<BR>it's right in the way of the frame rail On<BR>a Fiero. I made a manifold for my Engine block cause I used the electric pump under the front hood I wanted to gut a SBC short water pump and use it as a manifold but GM Has dicontinued the casting without that Boss. Every parts store I looked at only<BR>had pumps with this boss extruding. When we <BR>tried to use it upside down it was impossible  without cutting the frame so we abandoned the Idea and stuck with a Manifold at the front of the water inlets on the block.<P> Ray<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||10-16-2000||08:39 PM||||Mario, what's going on out there.... last week you sold a partial, second hand un-used V-8 kit and this week it's obvious that you are in the process of assembling one.<P>We all know you have (or had) the TR with the Zumwalt V-8 kit in it ..... so we know you you should be more informed than all your questions would indicate. Over the last couple of years you and I have exchanged many EMails and you've read everything on everyone of my web pages several times over. I've never recommended that W/P because it is not street rated. That Morosso W/P drive is for DRAG RACE USE ONLY, look it up in the Summit or Jegs Catalogs and you'll see for yourself.<P>You know as well as I do that that wimpy little motor on that w/p thing you posted up will not work for more than a couple of days in the Summer in SLC.<P>I hope this helps.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zorba||10-17-2000||01:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Mario, what's going on out there.... last week you sold a partial, second hand un-used V-8 kit and this week it's obvious that you are in the process of assembling one.<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Archie, not that I  feel a need to justify what I am doing to anyone but here it goes:<P>Yes, I am assembling a v8 system with one of your unused kits, not a copy, but an original that was offered me for a very good price because the owner gave up his project with a manual conversion. I was about ready to place an order with you when I had this opportunity. Unlike others, I decided <B>NOT TO BOTHER</B> you for support since I did not buy your kit and I am sure you will agree with me that I am being fair in not bothering you with questions.<P>Yes, I did have a V8 TR with the ZUMALT KIT but as you know, the zumalt kit is not like yours and its water pump was NOT upside down and it used some funky bent pipe off the water pump and down under the cradle for plumbing, which I did not like plus it made the hose too close to the exhaust...<BR>The questions I have been asking are speculative to find out what others have used with success. Your W/P drive system is proven but it is not clear as how you "weld the shaft into place" - I have not access to a mig welder in my garage and think I can't rent one so I have opted to use the ELECTRIC water pump option you have referred to on your web pages. However, I think the MOROSO WP does not delivery more than 19GPM when in comparison to a CSI or MEZIERE pump BUT, I have seen no schematics on how these electric water pumps work and, maybe you can post a picture of how you've used one.<BR>I am reading things here about placing the water pump where the spare tire is but specifics on how to do this,is very vague to say the least. All I want to know is WHAT WORKS AND HOW it works, where to get it and how to install it plus plumbing specifics and pictures. This forum has proven to be very informative so far. So, in case you were curious about my dealings and what I am doing, that's the story. I am pleased with your v8 kit engineering although I have run into some problems with the crankshaft pulley being too close to the frame rail, even with the 2" elongated holes on the frame...I guess I made them a bit too long...<BR>but I think I can fix the problem with some adjustments. Other than that, my project is moving along with questions on what to do with the original vacuum lines, vapor canister and I am now learning about what wire goes where to get the engine fired up.<BR>If an electric water pump won't work for me, I would like to order your wp drive system as well as the 4-core radiator if you will sell those items to me. I hope this clarifies my mystery...<BR>||||reg||1
